# Statistical Significance Example (Comparison)

This example demonstrates VCasT's `significance` mode: comparing two already-processed
per-member data files (Model A vs. Model B 2m temperature RMSE) and plotting the
difference with a confidence interval, to check whether the difference between the models
is statistically significant at each lead time.

## Comparison:
This step compares `input_files/modela-T2M.data` and `input_files/modelb-T2M.data` on the
`rmse` metric and writes the per-lead-time difference to an output file.

## Plot Generation:
This step plots the RMSE difference (Model B - Model A) vs. lead time, with a confidence
interval band (`ci`) and significance shading (`significance: true`) so you can see where
the difference is significant.

## Commands

1. Compare Models
Run the following command to compute the RMSE difference between Model A and Model B:

```bash
# Compares modela-T2M.data and modelb-T2M.data on rmse -> diff_agg.data
vcast config_comp.yaml
```

2. Generate the Plot
Once the comparison is complete, run the following command to plot the difference with
its confidence interval:

```bash
# Generates the RMSE difference plot using diff_agg.data
vcast plot.yaml
```
